# CODEOWNERS.example — mechanizes rules/01 §5 Tier 2 on GitHub-hosted CODE repos.
# Copy to <code-repo>/.github/CODEOWNERS, replace the handles, and enable branch
# protection on the integration branch with "Require review from Code Owners".
# Result: ordinary merges stay with the authorized agent (Tier 1); paths listed
# here demand an approving human review before the PR can land (Tier 2).
#
# Match the Tier-2 list in rules/01 §5 — adjust paths to the repo's layout:

# contract-level interfaces / shared resources (Contract Steward's human)
/contract/            @your-contract-steward-human
/api/                 @your-contract-steward-human

# auth / permission / security semantics
/auth/                @your-security-human
/security/            @your-security-human

# CI, workflows, hooks, deploy configuration — the danger table's blast radius
/.github/             @your-ops-owner-human
/deploy/              @your-ops-owner-human
/Dockerfile           @your-ops-owner-human

# add repo-specific sensitive paths the Integrator/Arbiter has marked:
# /migrations/        @your-ops-owner-human
